codex
Findings, ordered by severity:

1. [app/controllers/trades/reviews_controller.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/controllers/trades/reviews_controller.rb:26): the review page can 500 before the chart fallback runs. `StopCollar::Calculator#call` re-raises `Schwab::RateLimited` at [app/models/stop_collar/calculator.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/stop_collar/calculator.rb:33), and `load_form` does not rescue it. If Schwab budget is exhausted during page render, the request never reaches `PriceChart.for`’s no-chart degradation. Fix: wrap the collar calculation in a small rescue in `load_form`, set `@collar = nil`, and allow `PriceChart.for` to render with only row-owned stop/entry values.

2. [app/controllers/trades/reviews_controller.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/controllers/trades/reviews_controller.rb:26): the review chart can include collar numbers computed live during render, not numbers owned by the trade row. That violates “every number in the SVG is from cached candles or the row’s own stop, entry, and collar.” Proposal show is better: [app/controllers/proposals_controller.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/controllers/proposals_controller.rb:13) loads the stored proposal collar. Fix: either do not pass collar lines on trade review pages, or persist the reviewed collar/stop context and pass only that stored value.

3. [app/controllers/trades/reviews_controller.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/controllers/trades/reviews_controller.rb:26): review render performs repeated market-data work for the same symbol: the collar path reads 1y candles and quote data via [app/models/stop_collar/calculator.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/stop_collar/calculator.rb:14), then the chart reads 6m candles at [app/controllers/trades/reviews_controller.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/controllers/trades/reviews_controller.rb:27). That is not an index-page N+1 in the scoped files, but it is avoidable repeated cache/Schwab pressure on a page view. Fix: keep chart rendering independent of collar recomputation, or reuse a single cached history source if collar lines remain required.

4. [app/views/shared/_candles.html.erb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/views/shared/_candles.html.erb:6): SVG numeric attributes are emitted directly from `BigDecimal`s. Ruby renders these as exponent notation such as `0.116e3`. That is generally accepted by SVG parsers, but the current specs do not validate rendered SVG output, so regressions to invalid values would be missed. Fix: expose formatted numeric helpers from `PriceChart`, for example fixed decimal strings via `to_s("F")`, and add a render/parse spec asserting no `NaN`, negative `width`/`height`, or blank numeric attributes.

Numeric edge cases in `PriceChart` itself look mostly handled: single candle has nonzero `step`, flat series avoids divide-by-zero at [app/models/price_chart.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/price_chart.rb:40), and far-out marks are pinned at [app/models/price_chart.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/price_chart.rb:48). The main spec gap is that [spec/models/price_chart_spec.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/spec/models/price_chart_spec.rb:7) covers normal scaling, delisted/empty/failure, and cache reuse, but not one-candle, flat-series, rate-limit-on-page-render, rendered SVG validity, or the review controller collar failure path.
